RUNTIME AND BATTERY: BATTERY-ONLY ENDURANCE AND BATTERY PLUS SOLAR, 48 AND 72 HOURS (runtime.py, stream l3batt, MESHSAT-1357).
PROTOTYPE DESIGN: nothing built, bought, powered or measured. MODELED on a1elec's energy_two_pack.py through energy_basis.py's
set-up (pinned); other cells INFERRED from their makers' figures. HF and the tablet kept in every arrangement (a1mech
arrangement A). The author's analysis, AI arithmetic; not a qualified review and not the independent check.

0. REPRODUCTION: the 72 h mean-day runs of the both-kept lid (4S9P) reproduce energy_basis.out section 5's NOM and WE rows:
   yes

1. BATTERY-ONLY ENDURANCE to the kit's shutdown (each pack to its own 3.00 V line with the 5 % reserve), PS-IDLE-SPEC
   42.8 W at the pack terminals plus the lid path's standby drain 0.025 W where a lid pack exists; aged to 80 % (REQ-014);
   both packs at +20 C, then both at -10 C (REQ-046's discharge floor). The 35E: the model's chain (C_min 3.35 Ah, rate,
   mean voltage, the 3.00 V fraction, the cold factor 0.4124 at 1C, a lower bound at the kit's 0.2 A a cell). The lid's
   discharge path loss (V(AK) and the loop) is charged on the lid's share. No solar.
   D06: D-06's 4S3P of 35E (12 cells), no lid pack            usable  107.9 Wh /   44.5 Wh:  2.52 h at +20 C,  1.04 h at -10 C
   A35: A(i) base 4S6P + lid 4S9P of 35E (60 cells)           usable  544.4 Wh /  224.5 Wh: 12.71 h at +20 C,  5.24 h at -10 C
   A21-P45B: base 4S6P 35E + lid 4S6P INR-21700-P45B          usable  496.0 Wh /  342.7 Wh: 11.58 h at +20 C,  8.00 h at -10 C
   A21-50E: base 4S6P 35E + lid 4S6P SDI INR21700-50E         usable  537.0 Wh /  320.0 Wh: 12.54 h at +20 C,  7.47 h at -10 C
   A21-M50LT: base 4S6P 35E + lid 4S6P INR21700M50LT          usable  533.6 Wh /  310.7 Wh: 12.46 h at +20 C,  7.26 h at -10 C
   X-NH1: A35 + 1 NH2054HD34 outside the case (PROPOSAL)      usable  611.6 Wh /  252.2 Wh: 14.28 h at +20 C,  5.89 h at -10 C
   X-NH2: A35 + 2 NH2054HD34 outside the case (PROPOSAL)      usable  678.7 Wh /  279.9 Wh: 15.85 h at +20 C,  6.54 h at -10 C
   the 21700 lids: each maker's minimum energy x the 35E model's end-of-discharge fraction 0.937 at the lid's current x 0.80
   aged (INFERRED); the cold factor from each sheet: P45B 0.910 (read by eye from the Discharge Temperature Characteristics at 4.5 A: about 4.2 Ah at -20 C against about 4.6 Ah at 23 C to 2.5 V (INFERRED; no -10 C curve)); 50E 0.722 (7.5: -10 C 70 %, 23 C 97 % at 1C (4,900 mA): 0.722); M50LT 0.700 (4.2: -10 C at least 70 % of Whmin (0 C 80 %))
   the NH2054HD34: its rated 6.136 Ah x 14.4 V to 11.0 V (3.1.2) x 0.80 aged x 0.95 reserve = 67.2 Wh; its cold factor not
   printed as text, the 35E's 0.4124 taken (INFERRED, a lower bound); its discharge over-current trips at 8.25 A (the kit's
   PS-IDLE-SPEC draws about 3 A; a PA key-down draws about 10 A: a smart pack alone cannot carry a key-down)

